Description: Code accompanying Alarid-Escudero et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.1177/0272989X221103163>, which shows how to implement a
    time-independent cohort state-transition model (cSTM) of the Sick-Sicker
    model in R and use it for a cost-effectiveness analysis, including
    within-cycle correction, probabilistic sensitivity analysis and
    value-of-information analysis. This file records the project version and
    dependencies; the repository is not an installable R package.
